  "email": "aisha.khan@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Identify ticket sender, check mailbox usage and devices"
}

{
  "query": "Outlook inbox rules not working",
  "reason": "No provided article covers inbox rules"
}

{
  "hostname": "BL-LT-0105",
  "reason": "Rule out the laptop being offline or Outlook not syncing as context for the rules issue"
}

{
  "summary": "Reported: Aisha Khan (HR Generalist, user_id 5) says Outlook has stopped applying her inbox rules that sort mail into folders. Started about a week ago. P3, she is not blocked. Checked: account is active, no lockout or failed sign-ins. Mailbox is 24.4% used (12.5 GB of 50 GB), so quota is not the cause (KB-010). Laptop BL-LT-0105 is online, last check-in today, 47% disk free, no warnings. Found: no KB article covers inbox rules failing. KB-009/010/011 don't apply. The search came back with nothing relevant. Still needed: look at her rules on the server side (disabled, in error, or past the rules size limit, client-only rules, conflicting or stop-processing rules, any changes made last week), check whether the rules run in Outlook on the web, and fix them.",
  "reason": "Something is broken, no KB article covers inbox rules failing, and Tier 1 tools can't inspect or repair mailbox rules"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Aisha, thanks for letting us know your Outlook rules stopped sorting mail into folders. I checked your account, mailbox and laptop. Your account is fine, your mailbox is only about a quarter full, and your laptop is online with no warnings, so none of those is the cause. I can't look into mail rules myself, so I've passed your ticket to our Tier 2 team. They'll check your rules and get them working again, and they'll contact you if they need anything. Until then, your mail is still arriving. It's just landing in your inbox instead of your folders.",
  "internal_note": "Sender is user_id 5 and her account is active and not locked. Mailbox is 24.4% used, so quota isn't the cause (KB-010). Laptop BL-LT-0105 is online, checked in today and has no warnings. No KB article covers inbox rules not running: KB-009/010/011 don't fit and search_kb found nothing relevant. Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation id 1) to check the rules on the server side: whether they're disabled, in error, over the size limit, client-only, or conflicting. No fix was queued.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-010",
    "KB-009"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
